  "description": "Los Alamos chess on a board six wide and eight tall whose left and right edges are joined, with two fixed pairs of portals that work for one player each. Pair 1 is White's: White's pieces go in at b3 and come out one step beyond c5, in the direction they were travelling, never the other way; to Black's pieces both its ends are solid blocks. Pair 2 is Black's in the same way, in at b6 and out beside c4. Because the edges are joined, a piece can reach a portal from both sides, and then it comes out on either side of the exit: the player chooses. Nobody moves a portal and a portal is never captured.",
